{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:08:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-05T15:08:25-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-05T15:08:25-03:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Brian/Desktop/workspace/pizzant/src/modes/single.py`\nTotal Lines: 60\nTotal Bytes: 2586\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import time\n2: import cv2\n3: import random\n4: from src.modes.base import HuntingMode\n5: \n6: class SingleMode(HuntingMode):\n7:     def __init__(self, bot):\n8:         super().__init__(bot)\n9:         self.direction = random.choice(['left', 'right'])\n10:         self.walk_stamina = random.uniform(0.8, 1.2)\n11: \n12:     def execute(self, frame):\n13:         # 1. Observador Universal: Si no hay batalla, patrullar\n14:         if not self.bot.check_any_name_visible(frame) and not self.bot.is_menu_ready(frame):\n15:             base_t = float(self.config.get(\"ditto_patrol_time\", 2.5))\n16:             self.log(f\"━━━━━ 🌍 PATROL ({self.direction.upper()}, {base_t:.1f}s) ━━━━━\", \"PHASE\")\n17:             self._human_patrol(self.direction, base_t, self.walk_stamina)\n18:             \n19:             # Post-patrulla\n20:             self.walk_stamina = random.uniform(0.8, 1.2)\n21:             if random.random() > 0.65:\n22:                 self.direction = 'left' if self.direction == 'right' else 'right'\n23:             return\n24: \n25:         # 2. Batalla Detectada\n26:         if not self.bot.is_menu_ready(frame):\n27:             if not self._wait_for_menu(): return\n28: \n29:         # 3. ESCANEO UNIVERSAL (MANDATO 6)\n30:         self.log(\"━━━━━ ⚔️ SINGLE BATTLE ━━━━━\", \"PHASE\")\n31:         f_bat = self.observer.capture_frame()\n32:         shiny_found, target_name, all_names, slot_id = self.bot.scan_all_potential_targets(f_bat)\n33:         \n34:         # Log compacto del scan\n35:         names_str = \", \".join([n.upper() for n in all_names]) if all_names else \"NONE\"\n36:         self.log(f\"Scan: {len(all_names)} target(s) → {names_str}\", \"BATTLE\")\n37: \n38:         if shiny_found:\n39:             self.log(f\"━━━━━ ✨ SHINY DETECTED! ━━━━━\", \"PHASE\")\n40:             self.log(f\"✨ SHINY: {target_name.upper()} ✨\", \"SUCCESS\")\n41:             cv2.imwrite(\"shiny_detected.png\", f_bat)\n42:             self.bot.send_discord_alert(\"SINGLE\", f\"SHINY {target_name}!\", \"shiny_detected.png\")\n43:             self._capture_sequence(target_name, is_shiny=True)\n44:             return\n45: \n46:         # 4. Escape si no es shiny\n47:         self.controller.run_away()\n48:         self._wait_for_map()\n49:         self.bot.encounters += 1\n50:         self.bot.save_progress()\n51:         self.log(f\"💨 Not shiny ({target_name}). Escaped. [Enc #{self.bot.encounters} | Session: {self.bot.session_encounters}]\", \"ACTION\")\n52:         time.sleep(1.5)\n53: \n54:     def _wait_for_map(self):\n55:         esc_start = time.time()\n56:         while self.bot.check_any_name_visible(self.observer.capture_frame()) and self.bot.running:\n57:             if time.time() - esc_start > 5.0: break\n58:             time.sleep(0.5)\n59:         time.sleep(1.0)\n60: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":202,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:08:25Z","input_tokens":3176,"cache_read_tokens":110533,"output_tokens":641,"thinking":"**Analyzing Wait Function**\n\nI've been examining the `_wait_for_map` function within `single.py`. The focus is on understanding the loop's conditions and exit behavior. The `esc_start` variable seems crucial for tracking the wait time. I'm exploring the implications of `self.bot.check_any_name_visible` and `self.bot.running` within the context of the larger bot operation.\n\n\n**Clarifying Loop Behavior**\n\nI've zeroed in on the battle escape mechanism and the subsequent loop in `_wait_for_map`. The 5-second timeout seems to be a critical flaw. If an escape fails, the bot incorrectly believes it's free. The following check: `if not self.bot.check_any_name_visible(frame) and not self.bot.is_menu_ready(frame)` becomes a problem, because when in battle, `is_menu_ready(frame)` will be True. This causes a false positive, and allows the bot to begin patrolling.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\Brian\\Desktop\\workspace\\pizzant\\src\\vision.py","toolAction":"Reading vision.py","toolSummary":"View vision.py"}}]}
